$md="# Midtrans Schema Decision\n\nRecommendation: **OPTION 3 — separate gateway transaction table**\n\nStatus: design only; no migration, table, source code, configuration, or data changed.\n\n| Option | Assessment | Risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| Nullable `legacy_payment_id` | Small change, but legacy and gateway transactions mix | Medium-high |\n| `transaction_source` | Viable single-table design, but constraints and reports become complex | Medium |\n| Separate gateway table | Strongest legacy isolation, idempotency, rollback, and audit boundary | Recommended |\n\n## Recommended table\n\n`midtrans_transactions` should contain: `id`, `payment_invoice_id`, `user_id`, `order_id`, `transaction_id`, `gross_amount`, `payment_type`, `transaction_status`, `fraud_status`, `settlement_time`, `expiry_time`, `raw_status_snapshot`, `idempotency_key`, `source`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.\n\nConstraints: unique `order_id`; nullable unique `transaction_id`; unique `idempotency_key`; valid invoice foreign key; positive gross amount; immutable source.\n\nWebhook handling must be retry-safe with lookup, row lock, allowed state transitions, and successful response for repeated identical callbacks. Legacy payment rows remain untouched.\n";
